<meta type=article>
<title | Bare boolean authoring forms (#219)>
<author | The Enscribe Team>
</meta>

<config toc number-sections />

A bare boolean attribute means `true`, the same as the `=true` / `+flag` forms — and it is the
canonical HTML / eHTML spelling. `<config toc number-sections>` ≡ `<config toc=true
number-sections=true>`. Only a *known* boolean promotes; a bare typo stays unrecognized.

<section | Introduction>

A numbered section (1).

<sub-section | Background>

A numbered sub-section (1.1).

<section -listed | Colophon>

`listed` defaults on, so its opt-out is the signed `-listed` — kept out of the contents listing, but
still **numbered** (2) and rendered. (`listed` is listing-only; it does not affect numbering.)

<section -numbered | A Note on Method>

`numbered` defaults on, so its opt-out is `-numbered` — outside the numbered sequence: no number,
and the counter does not advance. (`numbered` is numbering-only; it is still *listed*.)

<section | Methods>

A numbered section (3) — Colophon took 2 (a -listed section is still numbered); the -numbered note
did not advance the counter.
